<title>USA: NYSE Unavialables.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavialables.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday that EG&amp;G Inc, Three-Five Systems Inc, Terex Corp, Starter Corp and Wells Fargo &amp; Co preferred F were unavailable for news after hours.</p>
<p>Corimon SACA was also unavailable for after hours trade, the NYSE said.  </p>
<p>After the market closed, EG&amp;G said that while it expects earnings for the third quarter to meet expectations of $0.30 a share, it sees a shortfall for the year. The company projects earnings for 1996 of $1.15 to $1.20 a share, versus expectations of $1.30 a share.</p>
<p>EG&amp;G also said that it sees 1997 performance improved by over 10 percent.</p>
<p>Three-Five said it expects a third quarter loss of $0.60 to $0.70 a share on revenues of $13 million, with 80 percent of the loss attributed to inventory reserves.</p>
